-- conversation.fenel — `Conversation` (PascalCase): the in-flight
-- form-fill conversation between a bot and a chat/user. Carries the
-- field schedule, partial value, status cursor, and hooks for
-- completion. TS-side codeName: "Conversation" (PascalCase).
--
-- The `hooks` field is an inline anonymous record (not a named
-- `ConversationHooks` atom), so the readable source selector
-- `hooks.onFieldFn` resolves to the nested leaf occurrence. The selector is
-- compile/load-time only; its Labelable target is the leaf Field UUID.
--
-- Static rows: none. Identity is registered from the Fenel directives below.
--
-- The `botId` field is `EntityRef<"Bot">` — note the PascalCase
-- phantom name (matches the PascalCase Bot entity codename, NOT
-- lowercase "bot"). Status enum is extracted as a top-level
-- `ConversationStatus` ADT because `|`-enum refinement is
-- type-decl-level only.
--
-- History: Phase 11c sub-step 4 (2026-05-24) deleted the
-- vestigial `CollectorConversation` entity + its
-- `CollectorConversationStatus` atom (no callers post-11c-3 — the
-- legacy `conversations` DB table was retired in migration `0042`
-- and `Conversation` (PascalCase) became the active entity).
--
-- TODO: the empty-record `{}` placeholder shapes (`partialValue`,
-- `fields: List {}`, `completionPayload`) are preserved
-- bug-compatibly from the pre-3d TS literals. AGENTS.md flags
-- `{$record: {fields: []}}` as a documented anti-pattern; real
-- schema design for these fields is out of scope for this phase and
-- lands when the in-flight form-fill state-machine gets a designed
-- draft type. Until then the placeholder shapes preserve existing
-- validate-permissively behavior.

-- A bare identity facet is intentional: ConversationStatus is a first-class
-- constructor owner even though it needs no human-facing metadata of its own.
-- The system-entity auto-registration gate keys on the lifted Codeable
-- instance, so this registers the existing source declaration under the exact
-- `system/ConversationStatus` owner without a second TS definition.
@entity
@codeName "ConversationStatus"
ConversationStatus = Active | Confirming | Completed | Cancelled

@entity
@label "Conversation"
@description "In-flight form-fill conversation between a bot and a chat/user. Carries the field schedule, partial value, status cursor, and hooks for completion."
@icon "message-square"
@fieldLabel "botId" "Bot"
@fieldLabel "chatId" "Chat ID"
@fieldLabel "userId" "User ID"
@fieldLabel "formId" "Form ID"
@fieldLabel "hooks.onFieldFn" "Per-field fn"
Conversation = Conversation botId: EntityRef<"Bot"> chatId: Int userId: Int formId: String fields: List ({}) partialValue: {} currentFieldIndex: Int status: ConversationStatus completionPayload: {} hooks: { startFn: Maybe String, completionFn: Maybe String, onFieldFn: Maybe String, instanceTypeName: Maybe String, asDraft: Boolean } startedAt: Int completedAt: Maybe Int currentFieldPromptSentAt: Maybe Int
